# What must not reach the image.
#
# node_modules is the one that bites. `COPY . .` would put the host's tree on
# top of the one `pnpm install` just built, and pnpm then finds a modules
# directory that does not match its store — it wants to purge it, cannot ask in
# a build, and fails with ERR_PNPM_ABORTED_REMOVE_MODULES_DIR_NO_TTY.
#
# It is also 273 MB that would be uploaded as build context and then thrown
# away, on every build.
node_modules
dist
.angular
.git
.agents

# Nothing here is a credential today. This is so that nothing here becoming one
# is a decision somebody has to make deliberately.
.env
.env.*
*.key
*.pem
